			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2520510">
									

<p>This is from quite a while ago, but upon re-reading it and the comments, I had something of a thought. So, SCP-319 was created by an associate and/or rival of Lord Blackwood in, presumably, the universe good ol' Woody is from.</p>
<p>What if it worked?</p>
<p>Sir Lawhead-Smythe's whole goal was to create a &quot;door beyond our universe&quot;; the fact that 319 is in the SCP's universe is an indication, I think, of the fact that it worked. What if Blackwood came to investigate after Lawhead-Smythe's presumable disappearance and was sucked into the same door that brought 319, which also transferred his consciousness into a sea slug. Given this hypothesis, this means that there is potentially another British-explorer-turned-sea-creature wandering around somewhere&#8230;</p>

